cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use bandsolver in published work, please cite this software and
  Newman's description of the BAND method (Electrochemical Systems, Appendix C).
title: "bandsolver: Newman's BAND block-tridiagonal solver in Fortran and C++ with Python bindings"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: John
    family-names: Bernard
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-26
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/jcbernard87/bandsolver"
url: "https://github.com/jcbernard87/bandsolver"
abstract: >-
  A standalone implementation of John Newman's BAND algorithm for coupled,
  nonlinear one-dimensional boundary-value and transient problems. It provides
  a block-tridiagonal solver with endpoint coupling blocks and a Newton driver,
  in Fortran 2008 (with a C ABI) and C++17, both accessible from Python.
keywords:
  - numerical methods
  - block tridiagonal
  - Newton method
  - finite difference
  - electrochemistry
  - Fortran
  - C++
  - Python
references:
  - type: book
    title: Electrochemical Systems
    authors:
      - given-names: John
        family-names: Newman
      - given-names: Karen E.
        family-names: Thomas-Alyea
    edition: "3rd"
    publisher:
      name: Wiley-Interscience
    year: 2004
    isbn: "0-471-47756-7"
    notes: "Appendix C, Numerical Solution of Coupled, Ordinary Differential Equations."
  - type: article
    title: "Numerical Solution of Coupled, Ordinary Differential Equations"
    authors:
      - given-names: John
        family-names: Newman
    journal: "Industrial & Engineering Chemistry Fundamentals"
    volume: 7
    issue: 3
    start: 514
    end: 517
    year: 1968
    doi: "10.1021/i160027a025"
